# serializer version: 1
# name: test_text_detail_matches_snapshot[DOC001]
  '''
  DOC001 summary-separation
  Default severity: warning
  Pack: builtin
  Enabled by default: no
  Preview: no
  Fixable: no
  Fix mode: none
  
  Summary:
    Report a Python docstring summary with no blank separator line.
  
  Explanation:
    A Python docstring's first content line is its summary. When a further line follows it with no blank line between them, the summary and the explanation run together, which most renderers show as one paragraph. Only Python docstrings are inspected; Rust documentation comments, Markdown, and ordinary comments are not.
  
  Targets:
    syntaxes: python
    kinds: python_docstring
    scope requires: None
    owner kinds: module, class, function
  
  Capabilities:
    STRUCTURE
  
  Policy/enablement:
    The `DOC` prefix is part of the default selection, so selection alone cannot express opt-in: each documentation rule stays inert until `enabled = true` is set under `[tool.stilyagi.rule.CODE]`. `lint.ignore`, a matching `lint.per-file-ignores` entry, or removing `builtin` from `plugins` removes the rule from the enabled set before it runs; a `stilyagi: disable` directive instead suppresses reported findings after evaluation.
    TOML:
    [tool.stilyagi.lint]
    select = ["DOC"]
  
    [tool.stilyagi.rule.DOC001]
    enabled = true
  
  Fixes:
    The rule offers no fix. Rewriting a summary is editorial, so no edit is planned and `--fix` leaves the source unchanged.
  
  Options:
    enabled
      type: boolean
      default: false
      description: Whether the rule may report for this configuration.
      constraints:
        - Must be a boolean.
        - The rule stays inert, reporting nothing, until this is true.
      variants:
        false: Keep the rule inert even though `DOC` selects it.
        true: Let the rule report on the regions it claims.
  
  Examples:
    The rule is inert until it is enabled
      source:
        def f() -> None:
            """Do a thing.
            More detail.
            """
      configuration:
        defaults
      expected codes: None
      expected exit status: 0
  
    An enabled rule reports the missing separator
      source:
        def f() -> None:
            """Do a thing.
            More detail.
            """
      configuration:
        [tool.stilyagi.lint]
        select = ["DOC"]
  
        [tool.stilyagi.rule.DOC001]
        enabled = true
      expected codes: DOC001
      expected exit status: 0
  
    A blank separator line satisfies the rule
      source:
        def f() -> None:
            """Do a thing.
  
            More detail.
            """
      configuration:
        [tool.stilyagi.lint]
        select = ["DOC"]
  
        [tool.stilyagi.rule.DOC001]
        enabled = true
      expected codes: None
      expected exit status: 0
  
  Limitations:
    One-line docstrings, docstrings whose summary is the only content, and regions whose source span cannot be located are not reported.
    Configuration, per-file ignores, and suppression directives can stop a finding; static metadata does not describe effective enablement for a particular file.
  
  References:
    docs/rfcs/rfc-0002-stilyagi-python-rule-api.md
    docs/stilyagi-design.md#72-python-rule-api
    docs/adrs/adr-0012-adopt-the-source-backed-builtin-rule-contract.md
  
  '''
